# Copy the parts you need into `.env.development` and `.env.production`.
# Every `.env*` file is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT SECRETS. This is a static browser build: every value here is compiled into
# the JavaScript sent to the visitor and is readable in devtools. Two of the
# three are printed on the page anyway. Use this to configure a deployment,
# never to hide a credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#
# WHICH FILE IS READ
#
#   npm start      ]
#   npm run watch  ]--> development     .env, .env.local,
#   npm test       ]                    .env.development, .env.development.local
#
#   npm run build  ---> production      .env, .env.local,
#   npm run verify                      .env.production, .env.production.local
#
# Later files win over earlier ones, and a real environment variable set on the
# machine or in a host's dashboard beats all of them. So Vercel's project
# settings always win over a file left in a working copy.
#
#   .env                    shared by both modes
#   .env.development        development only
#   .env.production         production only
#   .env.*.local            your machine only — a personal test inbox
#
# Leave any line out and the build falls back to a built-in default, and prints
# which ones it fell back on plus where the estimate form will deliver.
#
#
# BUILT-IN DEFAULTS, WHEN NO FILE OR VARIABLE SETS A VALUE
#
#                    development                     production
#   RM_PHONE         (707) 641-6198                  (707) 641-6198
#   RM_EMAIL         6mehedihasan017015@gmail.com       roofingsolutionsrm@gmail.com
#   RM_FORM_TOKEN    6mehedihasan017015@gmail.com       roofingsolutionsrm@gmail.com
#
# So out of the box, `npm start` sends test enquiries to the developer and only
# `npm run build` points at the business. These live in tools/generate-env.mjs
# rather than in a `.env.development`, because every `.env*` file is gitignored
# and would not survive a fresh clone.
#
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE VARIABLES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Phone number, in the form it should be displayed. The dialable tel: link is
# derived from it automatically.
RM_PHONE=(707) 641-6198

# Public contact address. Shown in the footer and used for mailto: links.
RM_EMAIL=roofingsolutionsrm@gmail.com

# FormSubmit endpoint. Start with the destination address; once FormSubmit has
# emailed you the random string that stands in for it, put that here instead so
# the address is not in the page source for spambots to scrape.
#
# Left unset it already does the right thing per mode, per the table above, so
# only set it when you want something else — your own test inbox, or the random
# string FormSubmit issues. Setting it to the business address in development
# makes the build warn you, since that means real test enquiries.
RM_FORM_TOKEN=roofingsolutionsrm@gmail.com


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: changing RM_PHONE or RM_EMAIL does not update the schema.org block in
# src/index.html, which is static HTML that search engines read. Production
# builds warn when they no longer match; edit "telephone" and "email" there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
